🧱 PART 1 — FOUNDATION: How ConstraintLayout Thinks
❓What problem does it solve?

Column/Row:

This then that then that


ConstraintLayout:

This is related to that.
That is related to parent.
Everything adapts.


Instead of stacking, you create relationships.

🧩 PART 2 — Core Syntax (must memorize)
1️⃣ Create layout + references
ConstraintLayout(
    modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize()
) {
    val (A, B, C) = createRefs()
}


Each variable (A, B, C) represents one UI element.

2️⃣ Attach element with constraints
Text(
    "Hello",
    modifier = Modifier.constrainAs(A) {
        top.linkTo(parent.top)
        start.linkTo(parent.start)
    }
)


Rule:
Every constrained view must connect at least one horizontal and one vertical constraint.


📌 Constraint Rules Cheat Sheet
You want	Use
    Center horizontally	centerHorizontallyTo(parent)
    Center vertically	centerVerticallyTo(parent)
    Under another	top.linkTo(other.bottom)
    Left of another	end.linkTo(other.start)
    Right of another	start.linkTo(other.end)
    Pin bottom	bottom.linkTo(parent.bottom)
    Pin top	top.linkTo(parent.top)


ConstraintLayout:
1. ConstraintLayout { val (a,b,c) = createRefs() }
2. Each UI element → Modifier.constrainAs(ref) { constraints }
3. Must give at least 1 vertical and 1 horizontal constraint.
4. Use parent and other refs.
5. Used for complex layouts.


🧭 1. GUIDELINES — “Invisible Rulers”
🧠 What is a Guideline?

A Guideline is an invisible line used for positioning elements.

Think of it like drawing a pencil line on your notebook and aligning everything with it.

🧩 Why use Guidelines?

So your UI:

scales on different screen sizes

stays aligned

looks consistent

🧪 Example — 30% from left
ConstraintLayout(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize()) {

    val guide = createGuidelineFromStart(0.3f)
    val text = createRef()

    Text(
        "Hello",
        modifier = Modifier.constrainAs(text) {
            start.linkTo(guide)
            top.linkTo(parent.top, 40.dp)
        }
    )
}


🧠 Now the text will always start at 30% of screen width.

📌 Types of Guidelines
createGuidelineFromStart(0.3f)
createGuidelineFromEnd(0.2f)
createGuidelineFromTop(100.dp)
createGuidelineFromBottom(50.dp)
